fux-vt-compare: fux-vt beside other terminal emulators[K
[K
An excluded package with its own lockfile. It runs fux-vt beside a panel of[K
other terminal emulators ("engines"):[K
[K
- engines linked into the binary: Ghostty's core (libghostty-vt), alacritty_terminal,[K
  libvterm, avt, wezterm-term and the vt100 crate;[K
- engines run as processes of their own: xterm.js (`@xterm/headless` under[K
  Node), tmux, and xterm itself under Xvfb.[K
[K
Every engine gets the same output. After each piece of it, and each resize,[K
each engine's screen is compared with fux-vt's, cell by cell, along with the[K
cursor, the modes, soft wraps, the title, cursor reports and recent history.[K
fux-vt fails a case only where the engines outvote it (see "The vote"). A[K
failing case is shrunk to the smallest one that still fails and printed with[K
the command that replays it. `bench` times every engine on the same[K
workloads. The corpus (`corpus/`) holds what real programs wrote to a[K
terminal, recorded by `record`.[K
[K
It is not built or run by fux's own gates. It needs Zig, a Ghostty[K
checkout, libvterm's source and, for the engines in their own processes,[K
Node, tmux, xterm and Xvfb. `run.sh` fetches the first three.[K
[K
No engine is the truth. When the panel outvotes fux-vt, the difference says[K
where to look. xterm's behaviour and the standards decide which side is[K
right. Some differences are choices fux-vt makes on purpose, and each family[K
below records which.[K
[K
## Running it[K
[K
```sh[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh[17C [5C# families expected to agree, 20000 cases, beside the panel[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh engines[9C [5C# which engines run here, which vote, what each cannot tell[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh cases[11C [5C# the named cases beside every engine, with each engine's mark[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh verdicts              # the families with a recorded verdict, beside the engines that decide each[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh matrix[16C# family by engine: % of cases each engine differs from fux-vt[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh bench                 # MB/s for every engine on every workload, and the corpus[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh bench --engines ghostty corpus   # each recording alone too[K[40;15H[30m[46mUnWrap[6CQuit[8CHex [8CGoto[8C      [6CSearch[6CRaw   [6CFormat[40;120H[1;94H4366[20C17
[37m[44mfux-vt/compare/run.sh --list                # the families, their status and reasons
fux-vt/compare/run.sh survey[16C# each family alone: how often it fails, and the smallest failure
fux-vt/compare/run.sh run --family sgr --family text --cases 2000 --seed 7[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh run --engines ghostty,libvterm,xterm   # any panel
fux-vt/compare/run.sh replay --engines all --size 1x5 'abcde\x08X'
fux-vt/compare/run.sh --no-reflow           # fux-vt set up as fux sets it up[K
fux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus                # the recordings beside xterm and the panel; exit 1 if one regresses
fux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus --show vim     # one recording, and fux-vt's screen at its end
fux-vt/compare/run.sh inventory > fux-vt/compare/corpus/INVENTORY.md   # what the recordings send
fux-vt/compare/corpus/record.sh [NAME...]   # record the corpus again (see "The corpus")
fux-vt/compare/run.sh --cargo test          # any cargo subcommand, in the same environment
fux-vt/compare/run.sh --cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings[K
```[K
[K
The first run fetches Zig 0.16.0, Ghostty and libvterm into[K
`~/.cache/fux-vt-compare` (or `$FUX_VT_COMPARE_CACHE`). It also installs
`@xterm/headless` with `npm ci` in `node/` when Node is present. The first
build takes a few minutes (Ghostty by Zig, then wezterm-term). After that,
`fux-vt/compare/target/release/fux-vt-compare` can be run directly.
[K
- `run` exits 1 if any case fails, and prints up to five distinct shrunk
  cases. Each one shows:[K[24;3H- its families and the `replay` command;
  - the fields fux-vt is outvoted on;[K
  - each engine's verdict and differences;[K
  - fux-vt's screen beside the first engine that differs (`.` blank, `_`[K
    cursor, `↩` soft-wrapped, `≠` a row that differs).
- `cases` marks each engine: `+` agrees, `-` differs, `!` abstains.
- `--seed` replays a run exactly. Every random choice comes from it.
- `--engines` takes names joined by commas, or one of:
  - `panel`, the voters, which is the default for `run`, `survey`, `matrix`
    and `replay`;[K
  - `all`, the default for `cases` and `bench`;[K
  - `in-process`.[K
[K
